+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Sub-4 ST-005 — CBM IRQ handlers (port of AVM cqm/grx500/cbm.c:2198-2805).
+ *
+ * Port scope (per the plan + CQ-005 A):
+ *   - 5 top-level ISRs: cbm_isr_0 / cbm_isr_4 / cbm_isr_5 / cbm_isr_6 / cbm_isr_7.
+ *     The 0/4/5/6/7 naming maps to the 5 DT interrupts at GIC lines
+ *     174/178/179/180/181 — line indices 0/4/5/6/7 within the CBM IRN
+ *     aggregator. This matches AVM cqm/grx500/cbm.c:2298, 2670, 2697,
+ *     2730, 2783 verbatim (per AC-005-1).
+ *   - 3 sub-handlers: fsqm_intr_handler / igp_cpu_intr_handler /
+ *     egp_cpu_intr_handler. Each ports its AVM counterpart at
+ *     cbm.c:2198-2226, 2246-2273, 2275-2296 respectively.
+ *
+ * Out-of-scope for Sub-4 (deferred to Sub-6 per the plan's Step 7):
+ *   - NO tasklet_schedule (AVM 2688, 2712, 2720, 2764, 2798).
+ *   - NO napi_schedule (AVM 2747).
+ *   - NO irq_set_affinity (handled in cbm_interrupt_init in Sub-4 already).
+ *   - ls_intr_handler (LS path — AVM 2228-2244) restored by IG-120 (ls_w1c):
+ *     W1C IRNCR_LS on the do_cbm_tasklet drained re-arm branch only. (Was
+ *     deferred to Sub-6 per IG-014; the drained-path W1C is the one that gates
+ *     LS re-arm latching.)
+ *   - The "disable IRNEN then schedule tasklet" pattern AVM uses (lines
+ *     2680-2688, 2705-2712, 2716-2720, 2757-2764, 2791-2798) is reduced
+ *     to a bare ack + log here: top-half ack only, no bottom-half work.
+ *
+ * LOGF_KLOG mapping (per the plan + AC-005-4):
+ *   LOGF_KLOG_ERR_ONCE  -> pr_err_once
+ *   LOGF_KLOG_ERROR     -> pr_err_ratelimited
+ *   LOGF_KLOG_DEBUG     -> pr_debug
+ *
+ * Naming-rename note (recorded as scope_deviation in build-manifest):
+ *   ST-004's stubs in this file named the handlers cbm_isr_0..cbm_isr_4
+ *   sequentially; the ST-005 plan demands cbm_isr_0/4/5/6/7 to reflect
+ *   the DT-line indices. cbm.c (outside this file_scope) also references
+ *   the handler addresses inside cbm_isr_table[]; that file is updated
+ *   in the same commit with a minimal rename. Recorded as scope_deviation
+ *   "rename forced by AC-005-1 — old sequential names break naming
+ *   contract; cbm.c update is mechanical".
+ *
+ * AVM source citations (every register read / write below cites its AVM
+ * cqm/grx500/cbm.c line range so the byte-exact verbatim copy is auditable).
+ */
